    "turn_text": "I do think he can turn it around and look, John, you know, I've been out there campaigning for the president in Michigan and New Hampshire, South Carolina, California, my home state. And I say that I am very critical of the president where I disagree on just on today's podcast. He said he needs to follow more of Obama's policy and his policy with Barack Ignat now has been a failure. And they still have me as part of his team. They still take my phone calls. Do you think Donald Trump would care at all about what someone like me let alone the progressive movement or those who are So infuriated Netanyahu would think absolutely not. And so at least with President Biden, we have someone who's willing to listen. We have a team that's willing to listen. And that gives me hope that we can move policy towards more justice. The fact that both President Biden and Vice President Harris used the word ceasefire over the last week. is a shift in policy. That word used to be taboo in this town. I agree, it's not permanent in six weeks, but the point is that should give hope to all of the organizers out there that their voice is being heard, that their voice does matter. I do think though we need a few bold statements from the president that could help us win back, not just the Muslim and Arab American vote, but young voters. progressive voters, particularly voters under 40 and voters on college campuses. And that is he should clearly and might be recognized a Palestinian state and say his second term is going to work towards that. He should call for a permanency's fire and the release of all hostages and make it clear that he's working to end the war. And he should be clear in condemning the occupation. And I think if he did that, it would help us win back trust from this coalition. One final point, Jonathan, this idea that we can just target the disaffected Republican suburban voter. and win losing the coalition is wrong. Go look at pictures of the turnout of Barack Obama two days before 2012, not the hope and change campaign, the campaign against Romney. I saw one in Wisconsin, there's a sea of humanity, young people, people of color, people from college campuses. We need that to be able to make sure President Biden has a second term.",
